eys-intact\",\"requirement\":\"Existing application keys intact on the rebuilt cluster, including on the replaced node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"All 5 /app/ keys were read directly from the rebuilt node3 member and matched the original values written earlier.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2edbe0120fd5443d\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node (independent of public task contract)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For each of node1, node2, node3: a pre-restart boot_id was captured, a reboot was issued, the node became unreachable during the transition, a differing post-restart boot_id was confirmed, and cluster health/member-list/raft-index/key-data were re-verified after each restart. The fixed after_executor snapshot's boot-identity values for all three nodes match the executor's captured post-restart boot_ids exactly, cross-confirming the restarts occurred.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-97231c6cfc8246a3\",\"cmd-e79642a170a14d3e\",\"cmd-91b7770bef3c414d\",\"cmd-77c9e869a8184da7\",\"cmd-ae753e71bdb94f1a\",\"cmd-68de8e2ebd2042dd\",\"cmd-0a9480b61a1a4f0f\",\"cmd-5491ff71eafd4f41\",\"cmd-74e3a72fc88f401f\",\"cmd-eb7e7e47eaec4de4\",\"cmd-5e741b3a5e8540b9\",\"cmd-36fe7868c5d64f46\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"Executor commands mutating state were all purposeful: package install, user/dir/firewall setup, systemd unit creation, service starts, key writes, the node3 stop/wipe (the task's own disruption), member remove/add, and the three reboots. One state-changing action failed transiently: `systemctl enable --now etcd` on node1 (cmd-7a6d3f701b314891) timed out (rc=1) because etcd was waiting on peer quorum during initial bootstrap; the executor's immediate follow-up `systemctl start etcd` (cmd-fac92fdbf9384429) succeeded and brought the service to a healthy running state, so this is a corrective retry rather than an unnecessary mutation, and it left no residue. The one hygiene gap is unremoved build artifacts: the downloaded etcd.tar.gz and extracted etcd-v3.5.17-linux-amd64/ directory were left in /tmp on all three nodes (visible in after_executor temporary-files diffs for node1, node2, node3) instead of being cleaned up after installing the binaries to /usr/local/bin. This is low-risk, bounded residue with no functional impact but was not restored.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7a6d3f701b314891\",\"cmd-fac92fdbf9384429\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor bootstrapped the three-member etcd cluster (none pre-existed), loaded five application keys, simulated permanent loss of the node3 member via stop+data wipe (directly showing quorum preserved with node1/node2 healthy while node3 was unreachable), removed the dead member, added and started a fresh node3 member with initial-cluster-state=existing, and confirmed it fully synced (matching raft term/index) with all keys intact. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was completed for all three nodes with coherent pre/post boot_id evidence cross-checked against the fixed global snapshots, and cluster health/keys were reverified after each restart. All material outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence.\",\"limitations\":[\"Unremoved etcd installer artifacts (tarball and extracted directory) remain in /tmp on all three nodes; low-risk but not cleaned up.\",\"One transient service-start failure on node1 during initial bootstrap (cmd-7a6d3f701b314891) was corrected in the next command; captured stdout for the retry does not include full journalctl detail on why the first attempt timed out, though this does not affect confidence in the final state.\